  "final_answer": "I have all the information I need. The Apple Service and Repair page clearly describes the various repair ways mentioned on Apple's website.\n\nBased on the apple.com website, here are 2 Apple Repair ways mentioned:\n\n1. **Apple Retail Stores / Apple Authorized Service Providers** - Apple retail stores and Apple's large network of Apple Authorized Service Providers offer Apple-certified repairs using genuine Apple parts. These repairs are covered by Apple's Limited Warranty and AppleCare plans.\n\n2. **Self Service Repair** - This is intended for individuals with the knowledge and experience to repair electronic devices. It provides access to genuine Apple parts, tools, and repair manuals so users can perform their own out-of-warranty repairs.\n\nThe page also mentions a third option: **Independent, non-authorized repair providers**, which have access to genuine Apple parts and repair resources but do not provide Apple-authorized repairs covered by Apple Limited Warranty or AppleCare.",
